Hydra does not redistribute third-party sequence databases. Each database it
installs remains under its own licence and must be cited separately:

  NCBI AMRFinderPlus  public domain   Feldgarden et al. 2021, Sci Rep 11:12728
  CARD                academic use    Alcock et al. 2023, Nucleic Acids Res 51:D690
  ResFinder           Apache-2.0      Bortolaia et al. 2020, JAC 75:3491
  VFDB                academic use    Liu et al. 2022, Nucleic Acids Res 50:D912
  ARG-ANNOT           academic use    Gupta et al. 2014, AAC 58:212
  MEGARes             academic use    Bonin et al. 2023, Nucleic Acids Res 51:D744
  PlasmidFinder       Apache-2.0      Carattoli et al. 2014, AAC 58:3895
  PubMLST             open data       Jolley, Bray & Maiden 2018, Wellcome Open Res 3:124
  Kleborate schemes   GPL-3.0         Lam et al. 2021, Nat Commun 12:4188

Run `hydra db info NAME` for the source and licence of any installed database.
